hebmorph
========

hebmorph is a Go port of the morphological-analysis core of Hspell, and it
embeds Hspell's Hebrew dictionary data.

Hspell is copyright (C) 2000-2017, Nadav Har'El and Dan Kenigsberg
(http://hspell.ivrix.org.il) and is released under the GNU Affero General
Public License (AGPL) version 3. Per the Hspell license, not only its programs
but also its dictionary files and generated word lists are covered by the AGPL.

Because this project is derived from Hspell's code and redistributes its
dictionary data (in a re-encoded UTF-8 form under data/hebrew.dict.gz, generated
from the original files kept under internal/gen/source/), hebmorph as a whole is
likewise licensed under the AGPL version 3. See the LICENSE file for the full
license text.

The English gloss table under data/translations.json.gz is not Hspell data. It
was generated for this project: the dictionary's stems by running
DictaLM-3.0-Nemotron-12B-Instruct (Dicta, the Israel Center for Text Analysis,
https://dicta.org.il) locally, then reviewed and corrected by Google Gemini;
the words Hspell files under its catch-all stem -- proper nouns, acronyms and
particles -- by Google Gemini 3.5 Flash Lite. It is keyed to Hspell's word list
and distributed as part of hebmorph, under the same AGPL version 3. It is
machine-generated and carries no correctness guarantee.

